/* book exam traps: Averaging reduces random noise, not artefacts locked to the stimulus. A time-locked artefact keeps its full size in the average while the noise shrinks, so it stands out more. | Referential and bipolar montages answer different questions; a broad field may vanish in bipolar because both electrodes see it. | EP latency is in milliseconds and amplitude in microvolts. Do not swap the two. | Odd electrode numbers are on the left, even on the right; C3 is left and C4 is right. | MEG measures magnetic field in femtotesla, not scalp voltage in microvolts. The units are not interchangeable. */
