/* book: lead: Biofeedback instrumentation turns a small EEG or EMG voltage into a light or tone the patient can see or hear. The patient then tries to change the signal, for example to relax a muscle or to increase alpha waves. The machine does not cure by itself; it gives fast, clear information. Clinics use it for relaxation training, stress management, rehabilitation and some attention training. Some syllabi */
/* book Figure 1.10.1: The worked example's loop: 20 µV RMS becomes 20 mV RMS, the rectifier and smoother give an 18.0 mV envelope, and the comparator with hysteresis (on at 15 mV, off below 12 mV) sounds the tone. When the patient relaxes to 12 µV the envelope falls to 10.8 mV and the tone stops. */
